{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/992742-using-garou-to-destroy-giovani-clan-werewolf-perspective","id":992742,"title":"Using Garou To Destroy Giovani Clan (Werewolf Perspective)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-24T20:54:11-07:00","id":992742,"title":"Using Garou To Destroy Giovani Clan (Werewolf Perspective)","content":"(Note: this is taken from the &quot;Hiring Garou Mercenaries in The Underwrold&quot; Thread in the &quot;Wraith&quot; Subforums; <br /> <br /> would just like to see how primarily-Werewolf Players think of this evil plan... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> The Giovani Vampires are infamous for substituting Gaian Spirits with Wraiths for their own Equivalent Fetishes.... Therefore...<br /> <br /> EUREKA!!<br /> <br /> I just figured out the QUICKEST way for an aspiring-schemer to get rid of the Giovani Vampires in ONE foul swoop!<br /> <br /> 1) Find the Kinfolk-Wraith of a Garou *Elder*, preferably their precious Little-Boy/Little Girl<br /> 2) Trick an over-enthusiastic/stupid Giovani Necromancer residing in the Clan's Venice Headquarters into binding that Beloved-Child into a Fetish.<br /> 3) Have said Necromancer USE said Fetish, record him in the act of doing so<br /> 4) Send nightmares of said child crying for Daddy's/Mommy's Help, with the Video Tape of the Fetish-Use sent by Fed-Ex to the door of the Werewolf-Elder the VERY next morning.<br /> 5) As said Elder is crying screaming and smashing furniture, point in the direction of said stupid Necromancer's closest relative<br /> 6) Wave goodbye as The Elder takes a band of *Champion* Werewolf-Warriors on a quest to beat-torture-claw and interrogate their way up the Giovani food-chain to Venice.<br /> 7) Grab a Coke And Popcorn, Find a good spot on the Tower of Saint Marco's Square Venice, play &quot;The Benny Hill Show&quot; theme music on a 10-hour loop, and enjoy watching the Giovani Clan burn.<br /> 8) See, wasn't that easy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> 9) Won't work with the heartless Shadow Lords though, because they *don't* love their family, or *anyone* period. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> How's that for a scheme, To Veteran Werewolf Players/Storytellers? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 10-25-2016, 01:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T21:02:10-07:00","id":992748,"title":"","content":"Well, Giovanni are too spread out and too well protected for a band of Garou to go after. If they irritated an entire Tribe though, like imprisoning every Kinfolk Wraith of a Tribe that they could find, then you would have 500+ Garou out for blood, which would cause the Giovanni to burn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T21:06:52-07:00","id":992750,"title":"","content":"Aside from the Shadow Lords reference, because they can be loving they just tend to be a bit aloof. <br /> Now aside from the fact that kinfolk and Garou generally speaking reincarnate this might work. A bit of tinkering and it would see a War Pack the likes of which even Gaia has not seen since the Banestorm.<br /> <br /> My tinkering to fix this into a workable multi chapter chronicle:<br /> 1) Ancestor spirits are disappearing. A local Sept is having more and more difficulties summoning ancestor spirits. An investigation is called for a pack is chosen.<br /> 2) The pack follows the trail in the Umbra and after a bit of time discover the missing spirits are being held captive the Pack moves the investigation back to the real world.<br /> 3) The local wraiths send dreams/or ST sends dreams leading them to a Giovanni compound that is housing the ancestor spirits as a way to use rituals to capture Garou souls.<br /> 4) The Sept gathers and storms the compound.<br /> 5) The Pack discover that this is one compound and the main compound in Venice houses even more Ancestor Spirits.<br /> 6) The Pack is chosen and sent to a conclave where they appeal to the Elders of the Garou Nation after much political jockeying a plan is formed.<br /> 7) Make popcorn and sit back and watch&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T22:48:32-07:00","id":992790,"title":"","content":"Ooh! Epic and well thought out! Thanks! (Takes notes)<br /> <br /> Hmm... only made that assumption because across the editions (including Kinfolk 20th Anniversary)<br /> <br /> 1) Shadow Lords are consistently described to only value Kinfolk who are smart/cunning/useful, and as a policy *don't* rescue imprisoned/captured Kinfolk as they are clearly too weak/stupid/useless to deserve a place at the table of Grandfather Thunder's Family.<br /> <br /> 2) In &quot;Kinfolk Unsung Heroes&quot; there was a horrifyingly-sad interview the Fianna-Kinfolk Journalist took from a Shadow Lord Kin accountant, who enthusiastically declares how she worships Garou superiority, and how she is *happy* with her inferior place in life, and is clearly *afraid* of her family elders; a product of abusive/oppressive brainwash rather than love and kindness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 10-25-2016, 02:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T06:11:16-07:00","id":992907,"title":"","content":"My response to every step of this plan is &quot;Just like that, huh?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T11:44:15-07:00","id":993031,"title":"","content":"Well, Massive-Pride and a SHORT Temper can go a *long* way in manipulating someone to do what you want when you want.<br /> <br /> Remember: *all* it took for the Black Spiral Dancers to manipulate the Garou Nation into declaring war on The Bunyip were a few Aboriginal Weapons planted around the corpse of a Red Talon Elder's Sister...<br /> <br /> ...reason and wisdom gets tossed screaming out the window as The European Garou did the Wyrm's dirty-work for him, and within *less* than a hundred years, the Australian Garou were no more.<br /> <br /> Stab a Garou where it hurts and angers Him the *most*, the people that he loves and cares about (hence why it's so hard to fight Shadow Lords, who as a rule *lack* this weakness), and you can play Him like a Violin, Overture Intermezzo and Bloody-Finale.<br /> <br /> What can be done to the Bunyip can EASILY be replicated on *any* Clan of The Children of Caine precisely because of the Garou's explosive Primal-Rage.<br /> <br /> Much as I admire and respect this Noble Warrior Race, I relate to the Garou the most out of all the denizens of The World of Darkness because of their All-Too-Human Pride.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T13:08:53-07:00","id":993058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/992742-using-garou-to-destroy-giovani-clan-werewolf-perspective?p=993031#post993031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Massive-Pride and a SHORT Temper can go a *long* way in manipulating someone to do what you want when you want.<br /> <br /> Remember: *all* it took for the Black Spiral Dancers to manipulate the Garou Nation into declaring war on The Bunyip were a few Aboriginal Weapons planted around the corpse of a Red Talon Elder's Sister...</div> </div> </div> </div>Retconned out as a post-hoc excuse used for the War of Tears. There are still plenty of other incidents, but that one has been altered, possibly because Rage Across Australia was so, so very terrible.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T13:28:56-07:00","id":993072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/992742-using-garou-to-destroy-giovani-clan-werewolf-perspective#post992742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> would just like to see how primarily-Werewolf Players think of this evil plan... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).</div> </div> </div> </div>None of it would work like this unless the ST really forces it to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/992742-using-garou-to-destroy-giovani-clan-werewolf-perspective#post992742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Giovani Vampires are infamous for substituting Gaian Spirits with Wraiths for their own Equivalent Fetishes.... .</div> </div> </div> </div>Where do you get this idea? Binding Wraiths shouldn't produce even half of the effects that binding Umbrals spirits can when crafting fetishes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/992742-using-garou-to-destroy-giovani-clan-werewolf-perspective#post992742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Find the Kinfolk-Wraith of a Garou *Elder*, preferably their precious Little-Boy/Little Girl<br /> 2) Trick an over-enthusiastic/stupid Giovani Necromancer residing in the Clan's Venice Headquarters into binding that Beloved-Child into a Fetish.<br /> 3) Have said Necromancer USE said Fetish, record him in the act of doing so<br /> 4) Send nightmares of said child crying for Daddy's/Mommy's Help, with the Video Tape of the Fetish-Use sent by Fed-Ex to the door of the Werewolf-Elder the VERY next morning.<br /> 5) As said Elder is crying screaming and smashing furniture, point in the direction of said stupid Necromancer's closest relative<br /> 6) Wave goodbye as The Elder takes a band of *Champion* Werewolf-Warriors on a quest to beat-torture-claw and interrogate their way up the Giovani food-chain to Venice.<br /> 7) Grab a Coke And Popcorn, Find a good spot on the Tower of Saint Marco's Square Venice, play &quot;The Benny Hill Show&quot; theme music on a 10-hour loop, and enjoy watching the Giovani Clan burn.<br /> 8) See, wasn't that easy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> 9) Won't work with the heartless Shadow Lords though, because they *don't* love their family, or *anyone* period. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> How's that for a scheme, To Veteran Werewolf Players/Storytellers? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>1)Most people who die don't produce Wraiths, so to start you are looking for a uniquely special kinfolk ghost of a particularly important Elder (one with enough sway to rally packs to his/her call, but not tied to any particular Caern.<br /> 2)You think it is feasible to trick a Giovanni that specifically lives at the clans headquarters into doing your bidding?<br /> 3)this one is even more impractical. The plan is to get said Giovanni on camera while they are out and about, and hope the use of the Fetish has some sort of visual effect you can record, and that you can prove a link between said item and the Wraith of the kinfolk.<br /> 4)send the Garou elder nightmares? how?<br /> 6)Elders generally have responsibilities they need to tend to and don't get to run around leading selfish crusades<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/992742-using-garou-to-destroy-giovani-clan-werewolf-perspective?p=993031#post993031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> hence why it's so hard to fight Shadow Lords, who as a rule *lack* this weakness</div> </div> </div> </div>You keep saying that, and I 100% disagree with you on that outlook. Just because the Shadow Lords take a practical view on breeding doesn't mean they don't love their family. That is a reall bizarre point of view imo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/992742-using-garou-to-destroy-giovani-clan-werewolf-perspective?p=993031#post993031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What can be done to the Bunyip can EASILY be replicated on *any* Clan of The Children of Caine precisely because of the Garou's explosive Primal-Rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>If this were an easy plan, it would have been done over and over in the WoD. Garou aren't a mindless weapon waiting to be manipulated.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T13:49:56-07:00","id":993081,"title":"","content":"Garou rolling up on the Venice compound.<br /> <br /> You get a Soul Steal! Aaaand you get a Soul Steal! And YOU get a Soul Steal! Everyone look under their chairs!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T14:08:29-07:00","id":993091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/992742-using-garou-to-destroy-giovani-clan-werewolf-perspective?p=993031#post993031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Massive-Pride and a SHORT Temper can go a *long* way in manipulating someone to do what you want when you want.<br /> <br /> Remember: *all* it took for the Black Spiral Dancers to manipulate the Garou Nation into declaring war on The Bunyip were a few Aboriginal Weapons planted around the corpse of a Red Talon Elder's Sister...</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because White Wolf phoned it in and came up with a really weak plot for touching off the War of Tears doesn't mean the impetus of your own stories should be similarly weak or farfetched.<br /> <br /> A lone vampire trying to manipulate a sept of Garou into killing a bunch of Giovanni might be interesting, but it should not be a surefire thing and would pretty much require specifics, not convoluted generalities involving ghost fetish ancestors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T18:59:11-07:00","id":993238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/992742-using-garou-to-destroy-giovani-clan-werewolf-perspective?p=993091#post993091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because White Wolf phoned it in and came up with a really weak plot for touching off the War of Tears doesn't mean the impetus of your own stories should be similarly weak or farfetched.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to hijack the thread, but often my first thought on stuff like this isn't &quot;this is weak sauce&quot;, but &quot;hmm, this is obviously a pretext, I wonder what the real reason is?&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T20:05:31-07:00","id":993268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/992742-using-garou-to-destroy-giovani-clan-werewolf-perspective?p=993238#post993238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't want to hijack the thread, but often my first thought on stuff like this isn't &quot;this is weak sauce&quot;, but &quot;hmm, this is obviously a pretext, I wonder what the real reason is?&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is an interesting point. I think that is a great response when you have to deal with those events 'in-game' and I take a similar approach to the War of Rage; rather than just saying 'well, the Garou were really stupid to do that, what a dumb bunch of werewolves,' I assume we just don't have all the information and there was something about the situation that at least somewhat warranted such a misguided response.<br /> <br /> However, at the same time, I don't want to get into apologist-mode 'out of game,' when things that really should have been fleshed out are sort of handwaved or glossed over. It may have been an attempt at granting the storyteller freedom so they can enumerate on the exact whys and wherefores of these conflicts, but I think a few more details (like what we got in Shattered Dreams) would have gone a long way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 10-25-2016, 11:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T21:43:07-07:00","id":995071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/992742-using-garou-to-destroy-giovani-clan-werewolf-perspective#post992742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Note: this is taken from the &quot;Hiring Garou Mercenaries in The Underwrold&quot; Thread in the &quot;Wraith&quot; Subforums;<br /> <br /> would just like to see how primarily-Werewolf Players think of this evil plan... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> The Giovani Vampires are infamous for substituting Gaian Spirits with Wraiths for their own Equivalent Fetishes.... Therefore...<br /> <br /> EUREKA!!<br /> <br /> I just figured out the QUICKEST way for an aspiring-schemer to get rid of the Giovani Vampires in ONE foul swoop!<br /> <br /> 1) Find the Kinfolk-Wraith of a Garou *Elder*, preferably their precious Little-Boy/Little Girl<br /> 2) Trick an over-enthusiastic/stupid Giovani Necromancer residing in the Clan's Venice Headquarters into binding that Beloved-Child into a Fetish.<br /> 3) Have said Necromancer USE said Fetish, record him in the act of doing so<br /> 4) Send nightmares of said child crying for Daddy's/Mommy's Help, with the Video Tape of the Fetish-Use sent by Fed-Ex to the door of the Werewolf-Elder the VERY next morning.<br /> 5) As said Elder is crying screaming and smashing furniture, point in the direction of said stupid Necromancer's closest relative<br /> 6) Wave goodbye as The Elder takes a band of *Champion* Werewolf-Warriors on a quest to beat-torture-claw and interrogate their way up the Giovani food-chain to Venice.<br /> 7) Grab a Coke And Popcorn, Find a good spot on the Tower of Saint Marco's Square Venice, play &quot;The Benny Hill Show&quot; theme music on a 10-hour loop, and enjoy watching the Giovani Clan burn.<br /> 8) See, wasn't that easy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> 9) Won't work with the heartless Shadow Lords though, because they *don't* love their family, or *anyone* period. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> How's that for a scheme, To Veteran Werewolf Players/Storytellers? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well...<br /> <br /> 1) So you need first a simple thing, like a character that knows about how the Giovanni works, how Ghosts work, and know precisely the Elder Garou that would behave like all that and at the same time have a loved relative dead that produced a Wraith and that the character also know where to find this Wraith. Because all of this is just the requisite to accomplish 1.<br /> 2) How do you do so? You have to find the right Giovanni, and it isn't as if the HQ in Venice isn't overprotected. This Giovanni should be powerful enough to make such a fetish, competent enough at family politics to be at Venice, resourceful enough to not have a master that could stop her, and still stupid enough to fall for your trick without noticing you first.<br /> 3) Well, it isn't hard per se to induce an artisan into using its creation. If you have enough access to this artisan, with you also didn't explained how you got. And then record the act, also not so easy, to end with the ghost screaming on camera, not a given at all for those &quot;fetishes&quot;.<br /> 4) Ok, at least it is feasible, once the previous stuff is done. Not that effects to send nightmares to an Elder fall from trees, but at least they do exist.<br /> 5) That not so much. How do you even find said relative, and then convince the Elder Garou that the relative have anything to do with anything at all? Not to say that you're pointing the Elder to just random people. If this could result in such destruction, the Garou Nation would have already wiped-out every single ethnic group on earth.<br /> 6) Yeah. It is all too easy for an angrily-crazy avenger to gather such a band. And then to such a band to simply hack their way up through a Conspiracy/Mob, because a surplus of Rage is enough to simply ignore powers and silver bullets, solve mysteries and crimes instantly, find the truth just with a glare to the scene, and them go on and on for months and through continents.<br /> 7) And obviously all Giovanni would gather at Venice to not give the werewolves the trouble of finding them through every hidden corner of the world and the Underworld.<br /> <br /> I find it hard to think that you were serious at this at all to begin with, but at least I had some thought exercise, if an absurd one. <b>Incbill</b> at least did a far more decent job, though it wouldn't go so far as to destruct an entire clan. It certainly would, though, make then enemies to the entire Garou Nation. Probably not all Giovanni would take part on it, either, but not that the Garou would initially notice or care.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T23:19:09-08:00","id":1028443,"title":"","content":"Hmm, after looking over the above advice:<br /> <br /> 1) Unless Emotionally-invested-in or Loving a Child on a personal level, No Band of Champion Warriors will flock to the banner of an Avenging Elder.<br /> 2) Having the Garou look for the clues and figuring out for themselves that the source of evil is Venice is impossible.<br /> <br /> And actually taking a look through supplements concerning the Giovani (and finishing heaving the contents of my breakfast just reading half-way), I remembered &quot;Necrophilia AND Pedophilia is so common in the Giovani that it would be RARER to find a Giovani who ISN'T a Necrophile or Pedophile&quot;<br /> <br /> This is going to take a cruelty, deviousness and sheer <b>viciousness</b> that only a mean-spirited Nuwisha can muster.<br /> <br /> Let's call the Nuwhisha Elder &quot;Wile E Coyote&quot; for the sake of convenience.... (Evil snicker)<br /> <br /> EVIL PLAN 2.0<br /> <br /> 1) Wile E Coyote observes and chooses a PACK of Lifelong-Friends, closer-than-blood Elder Italian Werewolf Warriors, EACH and every one able to take on armies single-handedly (Level 5 minimum, if not 6), and singles out the Homid Alpha...<br /> 2) Wile E. gradually finds and conspires to smuggle a Kinfolk with Pure Breed 5 into Italy, and through the Level 2 Nuwisha Gift &quot;Salaryman&quot; becomes another forgettable face in the crowd of Kinfolk at the local Garou Caern, and with the Level 5 Nuwisha Gift &quot;Friend Or Foe&quot; in conjunction with going above and beyond his duty as a &quot;cousin visiting from America&quot;, becomes a trused member of the Caeran.<br /> 3) Now, through the persistent and gradual use of the Level 4 Nuwisha Gift &quot;Pull The Heartstrings&quot; (Changing Breeds 20) he gradually causes the Alpha and the Pure Breed Kinfolk to fall in love and get married; heck, he even conducts the wedding ceremonies himself! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <b>4) 9 Months later, the Entire PACK of Legendary Warriors welcomes an adorable bundle of kinfolk joy into their lives, and Wile E Coyote, being like family to them, creates a life where *everyone*, Kin, Metis, Garou and ESPECIALLY the Legendary Warriors, love and dote on the Little One as if they are their own child, making sure he/she grows up to be the most pretty little thing while taking lots of photos with his iphone....<br /> 5) And eventually helps to create a &quot;annual family tradition&quot; where JUST Mommy, Daddy, Little Precious and Uncle Wile E visit a specific glade in Naples every year...</b><br /> 6) Then suddenly Wile E Coyote &quot;gets a call from his uncle in Brooklyn&quot; and has to go back to America... and 50 miles from the Caern, he shifts his face and heads to Venice....<br /> <br /> 7) Don Guiliano Giovani, on top of being a vicious bastard in the inner circle that answers to Antedeluvian Augustus Giovani himeself, is infamous for his taste in &quot;young lamb.&quot;<br /> 8) Wile E Coyote starts hanging around the Gondola Nightclubs and upon finding Kindred activity, conspires to become ghouled by one of Don Guilliano's Capos (Pretends to, of course, as werecretures are allergic to Kindred blood, so he keeps a bag tucked in his trachea so the blood won't reach his stomach). Since NOT every Giovani enforcer is actually a Giovani by blood, having &quot;hired muscle&quot; is not THAT unusual.<br /> 9) At one chance meeting at a Family Wedding Night, Wile E Coyote, playing the &quot;ambitious young muscle wanting to earn the Don's Favors&quot; role to the hilt, kisses Guiliano Giovani's hand and flips out his iPhone, and showed image after image of an Angelic Young Lad/Lass with a sunbeam smile and raven locks that causes Guiliano's eyes to widen like saucers... Of course, Wile E was smart enough to NOT tell him that this was a Garou Hero's Child.<br /> 10) Close to the annual &quot;Family Holiday&quot; He tells Don Guilliano the EXACT spot where he and the Alpha and his/her beloved child visits in Naples EVERY year, and during a routine Cocaine Shipping Session, &quot;accidentally&quot; drowns himself... but instead turns into a fish <b>(Level 5 Ragabash Gift: Thousand Forms)</b> and swims to a cove near Rome, and changes back to UNCLE Wile E.<br /> <br /> 11) That Year's July Afternoon, while Mommy and Daddy are flirting and frolicking, Uncle Wile E takes The Beloved Little Boy/Girl to play in a darker glade so Mommy/Daddy won't interfere, places a chloroform rag over his/her face, changes into a squirrel <b>(Level 5 Ragabash Gift: Thousand Forms)</b> and hides. He watches as Don Guilliano's awaiting dumb-muscle takes the little one away in their Black Ferarri. (Wile E. made sure he/she was looking the other way, so when he/she wakes he/she would not know what had happened)<br /> <br /> 12) Wile E Coyote bashes himself over the head with a branch, leaving a convincing wound and blood trail and acts unconcious. When the Alpha finds hims and frantically shakes him, he makes a big show of grief that he was knocked out and could not save the Little Prince/Princess in time, but was able to catch the License Plate before passing out. As the Alpha and her Pack of Heroes run in hot pursuit for their precious Child, Wile E Coyote changes into a raven <b>(Level 5 Ragabash Gift: Thousand Forms)</b> and flies to Don Flamingo International Airport...<br /> <br /> 13) The Garou Track the License Plate to Don Flamingo International Airport, to find that far too late that in his lust, Don Guilliano has <i>already</i> given the little one the Dark Embrace to be taken as his undead bride. (Of course, Wile E has been stoking the flames of HIS lust through choice words AND Gifts to make him take the HIGHLY unsafe trip OUT of Venice....)<br /> <br /> 14) In the ensuing firefight, Wile E Coyote drags an Enforcer with a cholorform rag over his face to a corner, slits his throat and takes his face (Level 2 Gift , New Face), and hurries Don Guilliano to his private jet while leaving The Newly Undead Little Kinfolk behind. After the jet door closes and it takes off, Wile E excuses himself to the bathroom, changes back into a raven <b>(Level 5 Ragabash Gift: Thousand Forms)</b> and flies out the landing gear doors before they close (think Arnold Schwarzenegger's &quot;Commando&quot;)<br /> <br /> 15) He flies back to the Caern, and tearfully (yes, Nuwhisha are good actors) watches as Mommy/Daddy hugs tight onto his/her Precious Little Boy/Little Girl one last time as the Sun takes him/her to the afterlife, weeping tears of blood and screaming that he/she is scared and dosen't want to die. As the Pack Of Heroes, who ALL Love the Little Boy/Little Girl as their Own is torn apart by grief and rage, Wile E Coyote uses Social Gifts to rouse the call to Vengeance. <b>Not to mention drive the Alpha and his/her pack beside themselves with grief by stepping into the Dark Umbra then into the Dreamlands (Level 3 Nuwisha Gift &quot;Shadow Walk&quot; is MUCH more versatile than &quot;Step Sideways&quot;) and creating nightmare after nightmare of the Little One crying for their help.</b><br /> <br /> 16) Calling upon all the Favors they can muster from everyone whom they have saved in the Long Heroic Life, The Legendary Alpha and His/Her Pack, ALL of whom <b>personally</b> loved the Child like their own and wants blood as well, summons an ARMY of Champion Werewolf Warriors to fly to Venice to smash and burn the Giovani Family To The Ground. As the fleet of vengeance takes off, Wile E Coyote turns into a Swordfish/Marlin <b>(Level 5 Ragabash Gift: Thousand Forms)</b> and swims post haste to Venice....<br /> <br /> 17) As the fires of vengeance light up the Venetian sky, punctuated with triumphant howls, Wile E Coyote, munches on a tub of freshly popped popcorn and slurps on a coke while listening to &quot;The Benny Hill Show Theme&quot; on a 10 hour loop on his iPod, watches from the safe shadows with a wicked grin as the arms and legs of Augustus Giovani (not to mention Don Guilliano's) and ALL his Inner Circle are torn off like a Chicken's Legs, and staked out for the Sun to be burnt into Wyrm-Ash.<br /> <br /> 18) Before the Alpha could set Fire to the Giovani Estate, Wile E Coyote silently slips a USB into the pocket of the Eldest Glass Walker; it is filled with a comprehensive database of EVERY surviving Giovani on the planet he hacked and copied from the Estate's Computer. After reading the files the Alpha roars in righteous fury, echoed by the approving howls of an army out on a Crusade to wipe the Mafia Vampires from the Face of the Earth.<br /> <br /> 19) &quot;Worth it! Here's to you, Gaia!&quot; Evilly Chuckled Wile E Coyote as he wore the face of a tourist nearby and puffed smoke rings with one of Don Guilliano Giovani's Cuban Cigars. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> How does 2.0 Compare to 1.0 (which as I said, was my FIRST attempt at writing a conspiracy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 01-09-2017, 04:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T07:52:42-08:00","id":1028546,"title":"","content":"It would be more helpful to have just added a link here to the other (updated) thread you posted rather than posting